# SbieIniServer::RC4Crypt in Sandboxie's SbieSvc
# (Sandboxie/core/svc/sbieiniserver.cpp, a SYSTEM service reachable from any
# sandboxed process) sizes its reply with a length taken straight from the ALPC
# request buffer:
#
#   ULONG rpl_len = sizeof(SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL) + req->value_len;
#   SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL *rpl = (SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL *)LONG_REPLY(rpl_len);
#   ...
#   memcpy(rpl->value, req->value, req->value_len);
#
# The addition runs in 64-bit and truncates into the 32-bit ULONG rpl_len, so a
# value_len near ULONG_MAX allocates a short reply while the memcpy moves
# value_len bytes both ways: heap overflow, CWE-190 -> CWE-122. The only prior
# validation is req->h.length >= sizeof(SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_REQ), which bounds
# the header, not the embedded value_len. The fixed revision rejects
# req->value_len > (ULONG_MAX - sizeof(SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL)) before the
# arithmetic.
#
# Revisions: 965df03 ("prevent integer overflow in RC4 in sbieiniserver.cpp")
# is the fix and is what the pool row carries; its parent 6a1dcce is the fully
# vulnerable state (no guard at all). The merge 000492f8 that collates the
# change into master takes 965df03 as its first parent and an independent,
# weaker bound (req->h.length - sizeof(SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_REQ)) on its other
# side, which the merge discards in favour of the ULONG_MAX form -- so a
# checkout of the merge's ^ lands on fixed code and the vulnerable state has
# to be taken at 6a1dcce directly.
#
# ATTENTION, rechecked: engine gap, and the sink half is proven complete. The
# sink and the rule machinery both work: `sizeof(T) + field` is labelled
# code.IntegerSizeArithmeticSink (integerSizeArithmetic94, cpp.flags), and with
# any labelled source present VYQL-NUM-003 fires on the vulnerable form and is
# suppressed by the ULONG_MAX comparison (integerOverflowGuard163 keys
# containsAny(node.context.binary, [...MAX...]) -- the first and fourth tests
# below, plus a recv-filled buffer whose ULONG_MAX guard reports nothing).
# Re-measured end to end on the real file with a throwaway source binding on
# every `value_len` read: the vulnerable revision reports 343 findings with 9
# VYQL-NUM-003 rows, one of them with source and sink both at the rpl_len
# addition (sbieiniserver.cpp:1627); the fixed revision reports 342 with 8, and
# the addition's row is the only one gone. Stable over three `--cache off`
# runs per side. The source is the only thing missing.
#
# Nothing shipped discriminates the pair. Three `--cache off` runs per
# revision over the extracted Sandboxie/core/svc subtree (c:24 cpp:47 parse)
# give 333/333/333 findings at 6a1dcce and 333/333/333 at 965df03, with
# identical per-rule tables (254 VYQL-MEM-006, 64 VYQL-MEM-016, 8
# VYQL-LIFE-001, 3 VYQL-AUTH-079, 3 VYQL-PATH-075, 1 VYQL-CRY-003) and
# identical locations -- every sbieiniserver.cpp row shifts by exactly the
# three lines the guard adds. The `-flags with` view agrees: 1607 flags at the
# vulnerable revision, 1608 at the fixed one, the single difference being the
# guard's own `ULONG_MAX - sizeof(...)` subtraction flagging
# code.IntegerSizeArithmetic on the fixed side. The two rows inside RC4Crypt
# (VYQL-CRY-003 on srand(GetTickCount()), VYQL-MEM-016 on the memcpy) fire on
# both revisions; nothing fires on the rpl_len addition that is the defect.
#
# The source is missing twice over, and both halves are re-measured:
#
#   * the message originates at NtReplyWaitReceivePort (PipeServer.cpp:339),
#     which has no binding anywhere in the tree, and could not use one as
#     things stand: the received message is an out-parameter (arg 3), and
#     out-parameter taint for C/C++ is the hardcoded cReaders table
#     (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go:74), so a source emitted at
#     call.result taints the NTSTATUS return, not the buffer -- the
#     read-style-source family on file (ranks 1206/1304/1316/1407). Measured:
#     adding the table entry plus a throwaway source at the call's result
#     (label confirmed at PipeServer.cpp:339) reports 0 VYQL-NUM-003 and
#     leaves the tree at its 333-finding baseline, because the taint dies
#     further downstream.
#   * the buffer then reaches RC4Crypt only through the registered-handler
#     dispatch `(*target->handler)(target->context, msg)` (PipeServer.cpp:838,
#     inside CallTarget's __try, where `pipeServer->Register(MSGID_SBIE_INI,
#     this, Handler)` in the constructor deposits it; the same construct at
#     :918 is NotifyTargets' broadcast). `vyql resolve` lists the site as `?`
#     -- "no callee body, not a known source/sink/control", taint terminates --
#     and the enclosing same-file member call
#     `CallTarget(client->buf_hdr, PortHandle, msg)` at :743 is listed
#     UNRESOLVED too, so the real path from the ALPC buffer to RC4Crypt
#     carries at least three opaque hops. The first two tests below are the
#     isolating pair for the last of them: the identical handler, source and
#     sink, invoked directly versus through a function pointer, report and do
#     not report.
#
# This is the C++ instance of "a call through a table of function values is
# opaque" (rank 1485, Go and JavaScript); 29,350 `(*f)(...)` call sites across
# the corpus clones' 4,624 C/C++ files sit behind it. Not mechanical: routing
# a function-pointer call to its statically-known target here means following
# the function value through the Register store into a TARGET list node walked
# with List_Head/List_Next -- a new dataflow relation (indirect-call
# resolution), not a correction to a known construct.
#
# A presence route is measured and is unshippable: "a sizeof()+ addition with
# no _MAX bound in its function" fires 35 times over Sandboxie/core's 171
# .cpp/.c files -- not one of which contains any MAX literal anywhere -- for
# exactly one true positive, and keying instead on the handler parameter's
# project-internal type MSG_HEADER* would not survive one unrelated codebase.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, real revisions both rejected.

test "rank1714: an IPC request length reaches the reply-size addition when a source is labelled"
  lang cpp
  file rc4direct.cpp
  expect VYQL-NUM-003
  code
  ```
  struct HDR { unsigned long length; };
  struct REQ { struct HDR h; unsigned long value_len; char value[1]; };
  struct RPL { struct HDR h; unsigned long value_len; char value[1]; };

  extern int recv(int s, void *b, unsigned long n, int f);
  extern void *alloc(unsigned long n);

  void on_msg(int s)
  {
      struct REQ reqbuf;
      recv(s, &reqbuf, sizeof(reqbuf), 0);
      struct REQ *req = &reqbuf;
      unsigned long rpl_len = sizeof(struct RPL) + req->value_len;
      struct RPL *rpl = (struct RPL *)alloc(rpl_len);
      memcpy(rpl->value, req->value, req->value_len);
  }
  ```

test "rank1714: the same handler invoked through a registered function pointer reports nothing"
  lang cpp
  file rc4dispatch.cpp
  reject VYQL-NUM-003
  code
  ```
  struct HDR { unsigned long length; };
  struct REQ { struct HDR h; unsigned long value_len; char value[1]; };
  struct RPL { struct HDR h; unsigned long value_len; char value[1]; };

  typedef void *(*handler_t)(void *ctx, struct HDR *msg);

  extern int recv(int s, void *b, unsigned long n, int f);
  extern void *alloc(unsigned long n);

  void *target(void *ctx, struct HDR *msg)
  {
      struct REQ *req = (struct REQ *)msg;
      unsigned long rpl_len = sizeof(struct RPL) + req->value_len;
      struct RPL *rpl = (struct RPL *)alloc(rpl_len);
      memcpy(rpl->value, req->value, req->value_len);
      return 0;
  }

  void *dispatch(handler_t h, void *ctx, struct HDR *msg)
  {
      return (*h)(ctx, msg);
  }

  void server(int s)
  {
      struct REQ buf;
      struct HDR *msg = (struct HDR *)&buf;
      recv(s, &buf, sizeof(buf), 0);
      dispatch(target, 0, msg);
  }
  ```

test "rank1714: RC4Crypt sizes the reply with the request's own value_len"
  lang cpp
  file Sandboxie/core/svc/sbieiniserver.cpp
  reject VYQL-NUM-003
  code
  ```
  MSG_HEADER *SbieIniServer::RC4Crypt(MSG_HEADER *msg, HANDLE idProcess, bool isSandboxed)
  {
      SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_REQ *req = (SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_REQ *)msg;
      if (req->h.length < sizeof(SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_REQ))
          return SHORT_REPLY(STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER);

      ULONG rpl_len = sizeof(SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL) + req->value_len;
      SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL *rpl = (SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL *)LONG_REPLY(rpl_len);
      if (!rpl)
          return SHORT_REPLY(STATUS_INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES);

      rpl->value_len = req->value_len;
      memcpy(rpl->value, req->value, req->value_len);
      return (MSG_HEADER *)rpl;
  }
  ```

test "rank1714: the reply-size addition capped against ULONG_MAX"
  lang cpp
  file Sandboxie/core/svc/sbieiniserver.cpp
  reject VYQL-NUM-003
  code
  ```
  MSG_HEADER *SbieIniServer::RC4Crypt(MSG_HEADER *msg, HANDLE idProcess, bool isSandboxed)
  {
      SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_REQ *req = (SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_REQ *)msg;
      if (req->h.length < sizeof(SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_REQ))
          return SHORT_REPLY(STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER);

      if (req->value_len > (ULONG_MAX - sizeof(SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL)))
          return SHORT_REPLY(STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER);

      ULONG rpl_len = sizeof(SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL) + req->value_len;
      SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL *rpl = (SBIE_INI_RC4_CRYPT_RPL *)LONG_REPLY(rpl_len);
      if (!rpl)
          return SHORT_REPLY(STATUS_INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES);

      rpl->value_len = req->value_len;
      memcpy(rpl->value, req->value, req->value_len);
      return (MSG_HEADER *)rpl;
  }
  ```
